I wrote the 2026-10-19 report, but it is thin and parts of it are unverified. No top lab shipped a flagship this week. The newsletter archives (smol.ai, Import AI, Interconnects, Last Week in AI) never came up in search. Most of the report therefore rests on aggregators or a single outlet, so coverage is probably incomplete.

- **Anthropic investor day (Oct 14):** It apparently happened, but I only found one post-event account, and it is opinion-leaning and partly paywalled. It cites 45% quarter-on-quarter growth and a negative market reaction. There is still no public S-1, and formal IPO marketing is still reported for the week of Nov 9. Treat the growth claim as a lead, not a finding.
- **NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Super VL (Oct 15):** This is a real, multi-source release. It is an open 120B model (12B active) with edge variants, and one source gives it an Artificial Analysis score of 26.5. That is far below the top open-weight models (GLM-5.3 at 45, Kimi K3 at 44), so it is an efficiency story, not a capability one.
- **xAI Grok Voice 3.0 (Oct 14):** Single source, unverified.
- **OpenAI:** A secondhand report says staff expect "one or two" new models before year-end, with the next flagship still gated on alignment work. I could not reach the original piece.
- **Unconfirmed:** Gemini 3.5 Pro, Qwen 4, DeepSeek V4.1 Pro, Kimi K3.x and the Mistral Large 4 weights are all still unconfirmed. I dropped two tracker claims that conflicted with existing records: a Meta Muse Spark item on Oct 15, and a GPT-6 Sol launch date of Oct 7.
- **Who's Ahead and research:** No changes to the Who's Ahead table, and no landmark paper met the bar.

I updated three other files:
- **State-of-the-art doc:** Only the overview note, the trend tracker and the changelog changed. The trend tracker shifted left, with Chinese labs and government involvement each ticking down. I did not file or resolve any predictions.
- **Memory coverage log:** Added this cycle's covered stories and the items I ignored, for dedup next run.
- **`open-predictions.md`:** Not touched this cycle.

Files are in `reports/frontier-watch/`:
