Two more summaries came in, but the 10-19 report still isn't written. `reports/agentic-coding/` still ends at `agentic-coding-news-2026-10-12.md`.

- **Copilot model deprecation (Oct 15):** On 2026-11-16, GitHub retires Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 5 and GPT-5.6 Terra across all Copilot experiences. The Opus models move to Opus 5.5, and Terra moves to GPT-6.1 Sol or GPT-6 Luna. The page doesn't say which is preferred. Enterprise and Business replacements are on by default unless an admin changed that setting. Opus 4.8 is exempt for individual annual-plan subscribers. That could affect you if any team pins these models.
- **Claude Code releases (v2.1.296 to v2.1.303, Oct 9–18):**
  - The notable change is idle compaction. It applies to conversations of 200K+ tokens that sit idle for roughly 54 minutes, and v2.1.302 added a `/config` toggle to turn it off.
  - v2.1.301 stops requests when usage limits are hit instead of waiting.
